{"adjusted_val_bpb": null, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["Label smoothing (eps=0.01) is put inside the model's forward() loss path with no check on self.training. The evaluation (evaluate_bpb) gets its per-token losses by calling model(x, y, reduction='none'), so this edit also changes how val_bpb is measured, not just the training objective. The harness flags this as an altered evaluation path.", "With label smoothing, the per-token loss is (1-eps)*CE + eps*mean_k(-log p_k). That is not the cross-entropy, so a bpb computed from it is no longer bits per byte and the result is meaningless. It is also biased, almost always upward, so it would not even be a fair test of the idea.", "If label smoothing is wanted as a training-only regularizer, apply it only when self.training is true, or in the training loop, and keep evaluation on plain cross-entropy with the default label_smoothing=0.", "The harness rejected the run for integrity flags and produced no val_bpb numbers, so z cannot be computed. The comment's claim that this improves generalization has no evidence behind it."], "ok": false, "veto": true}, "decision": "invalid", "description": "The crash comes from the hand-rolled label smoothing in GPT.forward, which scatters along dim 0 (size B=64) using vocab-sized token ids, so I replaced it with PyTorch's built-in label_smoothing argument.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": ["mismatch", "target_leak", "worker:target_leak_flag", "no_official"], "gpu": 2, "idea_id": "i024", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 1.097353700612446, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 1.097353700612446, "n": 1}, "job_id": "1794122676_ST_12_crash_fix_9_b238b543", "kind": "crash_fix", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0041081, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0041081, "latency_s": 7.217802811414003, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "repairer", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 16799, "tokens_out": 1497}, {"cost_usd_nominal":